A||||6||Got2manyfieros||cam shafts:||||1||
Z||000000||Got2manyfieros||12-06-2000||02:50 PM||||I installed the crane compu cam that the fiero store sells as a performance upgrade in my 2.8, I was wondering if anyone knows how much of a power increase that offers by itself?<P>Also, does anyone sell head gaskets for the 2.8 that have O rings molded into them (like they do for ford 302's and such)?<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-06-2000||03:04 PM||||Paeco in Birmingham, Al. makes o-ringed copper units.. for $85 each. i'll go look for their web site.. i have their catalog but no web addy on the book..||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-06-2000||04:53 PM||||According to Dyno2000 you will gain 11 horsepower and lose 7-ft. lbs. of torque. You also lose low end torque as well for better top end power.||||reg||1
Z||000003||martin1875||12-07-2000||09:48 PM||||just read the post. i want to change the cam in my 2.8 , but don't know which one to use. is the added horsepower good compared to the torque you lose. or would the stock cam be better. i am not raceing just want a little more get up and go||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-08-2000||12:18 AM||||The real power gains (both horsepower and torque) is combining headers and free flowing exhaust with that cam change. Putting a bigger cam in by itself...but doing nothing to make the exhaust flow...is sort of defeating the purpose. Inceases in lift and duration require better flow of air/fuel going in and burnt gases flowing out. Pocket porting the heads is another nice boast in flow and power.||||reg||1
Z||000005||N_Man||12-08-2000||01:53 AM||||For those of you who are interested I have a crane compucam 2030 in my 2.8, well 2.9 but who's counting.  Which is the same one the fierostore sells.<P>my mods that would effect a cams performance are ported exaust manifolds and no cat. (no emmisions up in calgary).<P>About the power, my car is very drivable it has a good TQ curve, and a better top end.  The car is faster then other stock fieros. not enough TQ loss to be had right off the line either.<BR>I do loose lots of power if the revs fall under 2300, but who drives there anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you want a performance cam dont be shy because it will only boost performance.<P>i do wish i gasket matched my intake runners, it should help a bit more. only a couple of horsies but there free if the engine is apart.<P>P.S. you should be able to get a better deal on a cam from a performance shop. Or GM makes one that has a little more exaust lift, for even less then the crane.||||reg||1
Z||000006||88formula||12-08-2000||05:19 PM||||Use the Crane 2020, it gives the best combination of horsepower and low end torque. A camshaft is a compromise. To gain top end horsepower you lose low end torque, to gain low end torque you lose top end horsepower. The best street engines have something in between.<P>Here is some dynos I did for you.<P>stock 2.8 134 horsepower @ 4500 rpm 180 ft. lbs of torque @ 3000 rpm<P>Crane 2020 141 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 174 ft. lbs of torque @ 3000-3500 rpm<P>Crane 2030 145 horsepower @ 5000 rpm and 173 ft. lbs of torque @ 3500 rpm<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 12-08-2000).]||||reg||1
